## 8. Workflow: Evergreen Design Docs & Task Cards

### The 2-Layer Hierarchy:
1. **Evergreen Design Doc (`docs/design/<slug>.md`)**:
   - The living architectural specification of a component or subsystem.
   - **Design Doc States**:
     - **`Open & Active`**: Currently has tasks planned, in-progress, or in-review. Work is actively being designed, implemented, or tested.
     - **`Open & Inactive`**: All current tasks are `Done` (or no tasks are currently queued). The subsystem is stable, but the doc **remains Open and evergreen**. New tasks can be attached at any time to reactivate it.
     - **`Closed & Inactive`**: Subsystem has been permanently decommissioned or superseded. **Only the human operator can mark a doc `Closed`**. Only closed docs can be archived.
   - **The Non-Closing Invariant**: Having 0 tasks or finishing all tasks NEVER closes a doc—it simply shifts it from `Open & Active` to `Open & Inactive`. Agents are **STRICTLY FORBIDDEN** from marking a design doc `Closed` or archiving it.
2. **Task Cards on the Project Board (`boards/<project>.sqlite`)**:
   - Discrete, actionable units of work added under the component's design doc (`--doc <slug>`).
   - Tasks transition cleanly through: `Planned` -> `In Progress` -> `In Review` -> `Done`.
   - **Tasks are NEVER marked "Closed"** (`Closed` is a design doc lifecycle state, not a task state).

### Pair Programming Protocol:
1. **Author the Evergreen Design Doc**: Reference or create `docs/design/<slug>.md` following `templates/epic.template.md`, structure phases into `## Implementation Milestones`, and register in `docs/design/INDEX.md`.
2. **Atomic Board Scaffolding (`sync-doc`)**: In the exact same turn, run `node harness/components/board/tools/board.mjs sync-doc <slug> --project <project>`. This parses the milestones checklist, registers the doc on the board, and auto-scaffolds milestone tasks. Never leave a design doc on disk without syncing its task cards to the board.
3. **Milestone 1 Protocol (Setup & Alignment)**:
   - Milestone 1 is ALWAYS: `Milestone 1: Setup the design doc and tasks`.
   - Milestone 1 authors the design doc, registers it in `INDEX.md`, and auto-scaffolds the tasks to the board (`board sync-doc`).
   - Attach the detailed implementation plan to Milestone 1: `node harness/components/board/tools/board.mjs set <id> --details "<plan>"`.
   - Move Milestone 1 to `🔍 In-Review`: `node harness/components/board/tools/board.mjs set <id> --status review`.
   - Commit the design revision cleanly in Jujutsu (`jj describe -m "..." && jj bookmark set main -r @ && jj new`).
   - Yield the turn to the operator for architectural alignment and review before moving to execution.
4. **Fast, Collaborative Pair Programming**:
   - No artificial permission gates or bureaucracy.
   - Tasks transition through: `⏳ Planned` -> `⚡ In-Progress` -> `🔍 In-Review` -> `✅ Done`.
   - To start a task: `node harness/components/board/tools/board.mjs set <id> --status in-progress`.
   - Implement changes, run tests (`npm test`), and visually inspect UI in Chrome via DevTools MCP.
   - When ready for operator review: `node harness/components/board/tools/board.mjs set <id> --status review`.
   - Once verified and approved: `node harness/components/board/tools/board.mjs set <id> --status done`.
5. **Fold-Back on Landing**: Update `docs/system/ARCHITECTURE.md` if schemas changed, and update the evergreen design doc (`docs/design/<slug>.md`). The doc shifts from `Open & Active` to `Open & Inactive`.

### Adding New Work to an Existing Design Doc (Rounds)
A design doc is the source of understanding for its area. Read it first, then extend it. Never rewrite it from scratch.
- **Architecture sections describe the current state**: Context, Goals, Design, and Verification are edited in place so they always match the shipped system. Update them when a round lands.
- **Milestones are the work history**: `## Implementation Milestones` holds one `### Round N — YYYY-MM-DD: <title>` block per round of work. Append a new round for new work. **Never delete, reorder, or edit earlier rounds** — checked-off milestones stay as the record of what was built and why.
- **Every round starts with Milestone 1: Setup**: The Milestone 1 Protocol above applies to each round (attach the plan, move to In-Review, yield for alignment).
- **Then sync**: Run `board sync-doc <slug>` in the same turn. It scaffolds only the new round's unchecked milestones; existing tasks are untouched.
- **Bloat means a new doc**: When a doc grows past a handful of rounds or the architecture sections no longer read as one design, author a new design doc for the new direction, link the two in `INDEX.md`, and leave the old doc Open & Inactive. Only the operator closes a doc.

### UX Execution Standard: Never Build Blind
All UX, frontend, web viewer, and UI tasks must be done with Chrome to check as you create. UXs should never be built blind:
- **Live Chrome Inspection**: Launch and inspect the interface in Chrome (using DevTools or browser subagents) continuously as you create, style, and structure elements.
- **Interactive Verification**: Actively exercise interactive flows (clicking buttons, switching tabs/views, modal/dropdown states, live data reloads) in the browser before marking any UX task complete.
- **Visual Integrity & Polish**: Confirm layouts, spacing, color contrasts, typography, and responsive resizing visually in the live browser rather than assuming static correctness.

